      "problem": "Factor $1-{j}^{3/2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The difference of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}-{b}^{3}=(a-b)({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a difference of cubes:\n\n$$\n1-{j}^{3/2}={1}^{3}-{({j}^{1/2})}^{3}={1}^{3}-{(\\sqrt{j})}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the given expression using the difference of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-{j}^{3/2} & ={1}^{3}-{(\\sqrt{j})}^{3} \\\\  & =(1-\\sqrt{j})({1}^{2}+1\\cdot \\sqrt{j}+(\\sqrt{j})^{2}) \\\\  & =(1-\\sqrt{j})(1+\\sqrt{j}+j)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
